From: eirikr <iamhumanipromise1010101@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:50:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] pl022: report receive FIFO not-empty and full with the
 PrimeCell polarity

SSPSR bit 2 (RNE) is set while the receive FIFO holds data and bit 3 (RFF)
while it is full (RP2040 datasheet section 4.4.4, SSPSR). The model returned
RNE for an empty FIFO and RFF for one with room, so the standard drain loop
"while (SSPSR & RNE) read SSPDR" never ended on an idle controller: the
PicoCalc console driver's spi_wait_idle() spins in it from its first panel
command. SSPDR returned data and dequeued only while the FIFO was not full,
so a full FIFO could never be read. SSPDR now dequeues whenever an entry
exists, and the two status bits follow the datasheet.
---
 emulation/peripherals/spi/rp2040_spi.cs | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/emulation/peripherals/spi/rp2040_spi.cs b/emulation/peripherals/spi/rp2040_spi.cs
index 3dd86e4..2ab0acf 100644
--- a/emulation/peripherals/spi/rp2040_spi.cs
+++ b/emulation/peripherals/spi/rp2040_spi.cs
@@ -352,10 +352,9 @@ namespace Antmicro.Renode.Peripherals.SPI
       Registers.SSPDR.Define(registers)
         .WithValueField(0, 16, valueProviderCallback: _ =>
         {
-          if (rxBuffer.Count < rxBuffer.Capacity)
+          ushort ret;
+          if (rxBuffer.TryDequeue(out ret))
           {
-            ushort ret;
-            rxBuffer.TryDequeue(out ret);
             return ret;
           }
           return 0;
@@ -376,8 +375,8 @@ namespace Antmicro.Renode.Peripherals.SPI
       Registers.SSPSR.Define(registers)
         .WithFlag(0, FieldMode.Read, valueProviderCallback: _ => txBuffer.Count == 0, name: "SSPSR_TFE")
         .WithFlag(1, FieldMode.Read, valueProviderCallback: _ => txBuffer.Count != txBuffer.Capacity, name: "SSPSR_TNF")
-        .WithFlag(2, FieldMode.Read, valueProviderCallback: _ => rxBuffer.Count == 0, name: "SSPSR_RNE")
-        .WithFlag(3, FieldMode.Read, valueProviderCallback: _ => rxBuffer.Count != rxBuffer.Capacity, name: "SSPSR_RFF")
+        .WithFlag(2, FieldMode.Read, valueProviderCallback: _ => rxBuffer.Count != 0, name: "SSPSR_RNE")
+        .WithFlag(3, FieldMode.Read, valueProviderCallback: _ => rxBuffer.Count == rxBuffer.Capacity, name: "SSPSR_RFF")
         .WithFlag(4, FieldMode.Read, valueProviderCallback: _ => running, name: "SSPSR_BSY");
 
       Registers.SSPCPSR.Define(registers)
